-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 11 (OFFENCES AND PENALTIES, ss 46 to 58).
-- A section that makes a contravention an offence takes the RESULT of the rule that says what the contravention is
-- (s 46 takes the result of s 8(1); s 47 the result of s 20(1)), and returns what the section says about guilt, the
-- ceilings on punishment, forfeiture, and compounding. The ceilings are Punishment records (sgba-nouns.l4); "or to both" means
-- the court may impose either or both, within each ceiling.

§ `46. Offences relating to licensable broadcasting services`

-- src:3666 | 46. Any person who contravenes section 8(1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:3667 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:3668 | $200,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to
-- src:3669 | both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:3670 | exceeding $10,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:3671 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 46 (guilt) (src:3666-3671)
-- x is the result of `s 8(1) the person provides a licensable broadcasting service without the licence the subsection requires, on`.
GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS x

-- src:3666 | 46. Any person who contravenes section 8(1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:3667 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:3668 | $200,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to
-- src:3669 | both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:3670 | exceeding $10,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:3671 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 46 (punishment) (src:3666-3671)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 46 the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 200000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `imprisonment not exceeding` 36
                  , `daily fine` IS `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` 10000
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

§ `47. Offences relating to installation, sale, import or possession of broadcasting apparatus`

-- src:3676 | 47. Any person who contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c) shall be
-- src:3677 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3678 | exceeding $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3
-- src:3679 | years or to both, and any broadcasting apparatus installed or found in
@ref s 47 (guilt) (src:3676-3679)
-- x is the result of `s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), on`.
GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS x

-- src:3676 | 47. Any person who contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c) shall be
-- src:3677 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3678 | exceeding $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3
-- src:3679 | years or to both, and any broadcasting apparatus installed or found in
-- src:3680 | the possession of the person so convicted shall be forfeited to the
-- src:3681 | Authority.
@ref s 47 (punishment) (src:3676-3681)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 47 the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 40000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `imprisonment not exceeding` 36
                  , `daily fine` IS `no further daily fine is provided`
                  , `forfeiture` IS `the apparatus installed or found in the possession of the person convicted is forfeited to the Authority`

-- src:3679 | years or to both, and any broadcasting apparatus installed or found in
-- src:3680 | the possession of the person so convicted shall be forfeited to the
-- src:3681 | Authority.
@ref s 47 (forfeiture) (src:3679-3681)
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of an offence under section 47` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the apparatus is installed, or found in the possession of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47 the apparatus is forfeited to the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the person has been convicted of an offence under section 47` THEN JUST `the apparatus is installed, or found in the possession of the person` ELSE NOTHING

§ `48. Offences relating to unauthorised decoders and unauthorised reception of encrypted programmes`

-- src:3686 | 48.—(1) A person must not manufacture, assemble, modify,
-- src:3687 | import, export, sell, offer for sale, let for hire or otherwise
-- src:3688 | distribute any decoder which the person knows is an unauthorised
-- src:3689 | decoder.
@ref s 48(1) (src:3686-3689)
GIVEN act IS A `Act with a decoder`
      `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited` MEANS
    `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` AND `the person knows the decoder is an unauthorised decoder`
    AND (CONSIDER act
         WHEN `manufacture` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `assemble` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `modify` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `import` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `export` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `sell` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `offer for sale` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `let for hire` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `otherwise distribute` THEN TRUE)

-- src:3694 | (2) A person must not wilfully receive or rebroadcast any encrypted
-- src:3695 | programme which has been decoded without the authorisation of the
-- src:3696 | lawful provider of a broadcasting service who had broadcast the
-- src:3697 | programme.
@ref s 48(2) (src:3694-3697)
GIVEN `the person wilfully receives or rebroadcasts the encrypted programme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme has been decoded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decoding was with the authorisation of the lawful provider of the broadcasting service who had broadcast the programme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(2) the person's reception or rebroadcast is prohibited` MEANS
    `the person wilfully receives or rebroadcasts the encrypted programme` AND `the programme has been decoded` AND (NOT `the decoding was with the authorisation of the lawful provider of the broadcasting service who had broadcast the programme`)

-- src:3699 | (3) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) shall be
-- src:3700 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3701 | exceeding $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:3702 | 3 years or to both, and any unauthorised decoder shall be forfeited to
-- src:3703 | the Authority.
@ref s 48(3) (guilt) (src:3699-3703)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person contravenes subsection (1) or (2)`

-- src:3699 | (3) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) shall be
-- src:3700 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3701 | exceeding $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:3702 | 3 years or to both, and any unauthorised decoder shall be forfeited to
-- src:3703 | the Authority.
@ref s 48(3) (punishment) (src:3699-3703)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 48(3) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 40000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `imprisonment not exceeding` 36
                  , `daily fine` IS `no further daily fine is provided`
                  , `forfeiture` IS `the unauthorised decoder is forfeited to the Authority`

-- src:3705 | (4) Where it is proved that a person has manufactured, assembled,
-- src:3706 | modified, imported, exported, sold, offered for sale, let for hire or
-- src:3707 | otherwise distributed any unauthorised decoder, it is presumed,
-- src:3708 | unless there is evidence to the contrary, that the person knew that the
-- src:3709 | decoder was an unauthorised decoder.
@ref s 48(4) (src:3705-3709)
-- A presumption that holds "unless there is evidence to the contrary": whether the evidence is enough is for the court (asked as a fact).
GIVEN `it is proved that the person did the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(4) it is presumed that the person knew that the decoder was an unauthorised decoder` MEANS
    IF `it is proved that the person did the act` AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3711 | (5) In this section and section 48A —
-- src:3713 | “decoder” means any apparatus or device (including a computer
-- src:3714 | program) or any component or part thereof which is designed
-- src:3715 | or adapted to enable (whether on its own or with any other
-- src:3716 | apparatus or device) an encrypted programme to be decoded;
@ref s 48(5) chapeau and "decoder" (src:3711-3716)
GIVEN `it is an apparatus or device (including a computer program), or a component or part of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed or adapted to enable an encrypted programme to be decoded, on its own or with another apparatus or device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(5) the thing is a decoder` MEANS
    `it is an apparatus or device (including a computer program), or a component or part of one` AND `it is designed or adapted to enable an encrypted programme to be decoded, on its own or with another apparatus or device`

-- src:3718 | “lawful provider”, in relation to a broadcasting service,
-- src:3719 | means —
-- src:3721 | (a) a person who holds a broadcasting licence; or
-- src:3723 | (b) in the case of a broadcasting service transmitted from
-- src:3724 | a place outside Singapore, the person who is
-- src:3725 | authorised to provide the broadcasting service in
-- src:3726 | accordance with the laws of that place;
@ref s 48(5) "lawful provider" (src:3718-3726)
GIVEN `the person holds a broadcasting licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is transmitted from a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised to provide the service in accordance with the laws of that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(5) the person is the lawful provider in relation to the broadcasting service` MEANS
    `the person holds a broadcasting licence` OR (`the service is transmitted from a place outside Singapore` AND `the person is authorised to provide the service in accordance with the laws of that place`)

-- src:3728 | “unauthorised decoder” means a decoder which is designed or
-- src:3729 | adapted to enable an encrypted programme to be viewed in
-- src:3730 | decoded form without the authorisation of the lawful
-- src:3731 | provider of a broadcasting service who had broadcast the
-- src:3732 | programme.
@ref s 48(5) "unauthorised decoder" (src:3728-3732)
GIVEN `it is a decoder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed or adapted to enable an encrypted programme to be viewed in decoded form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is without the authorisation of the lawful provider of the broadcasting service who had broadcast the programme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(5) the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` MEANS
    `it is a decoder` AND `it is designed or adapted to enable an encrypted programme to be viewed in decoded form` AND `that is without the authorisation of the lawful provider of the broadcasting service who had broadcast the programme`

§ `48A. Civil action in relation to unauthorised decoders and decoded programmes`

-- src:3740 | 48A.—(1) Where —
-- src:3742 | (a) a person does an act mentioned in section 48(1) in relation
-- src:3743 | to an unauthorised decoder;
-- src:3745 | (b) the unauthorised decoder is used to decode an encrypted
-- src:3746 | programme; and
-- src:3748 | (c) the lawful provider of a broadcasting service who had
-- src:3749 | broadcast the encrypted programme or the owner of the
-- src:3750 | copyright in the programme has thereby suffered any loss
-- src:3751 | or damage,
-- src:3753 | the lawful provider of the broadcasting service or the owner of the
-- src:3754 | copyright in the programme (as the case may be) may bring a civil
-- src:3755 | action against the person mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 48A(1) (src:3740-3755)
GIVEN `the person does an act mentioned in section 48(1) in relation to an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unauthorised decoder is used to decode an encrypted programme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawful provider or the owner of the copyright in the programme has thereby suffered loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48A(1) the lawful provider or the copyright owner may bring a civil action against the person` MEANS
    `the person does an act mentioned in section 48(1) in relation to an unauthorised decoder` AND `the unauthorised decoder is used to decode an encrypted programme` AND `the lawful provider or the owner of the copyright in the programme has thereby suffered loss or damage`

-- src:3757 | (2) Where —
-- src:3759 | (a) a person does an act mentioned in section 48(2) in relation
-- src:3760 | to an encrypted programme that has been decoded without
-- src:3761 | the authorisation of the lawful provider of a broadcasting
-- src:3762 | service who had broadcast the programme; and
-- src:3764 | (b) the lawful provider of the broadcasting service or the
-- src:3765 | owner of the copyright in the programme has thereby
-- src:3766 | suffered any loss or damage,
-- src:3768 | the lawful provider of the broadcasting service or the owner of the
-- src:3769 | copyright in the programme (as the case may be) may bring a civil
-- src:3770 | action against the person mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 48A(2) (src:3757-3770)
GIVEN `the person does an act mentioned in section 48(2) in relation to an encrypted programme that has been decoded without the lawful provider's authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawful provider or the owner of the copyright in the programme has thereby suffered loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48A(2) the lawful provider or the copyright owner may bring a civil action against the person` MEANS
    `the person does an act mentioned in section 48(2) in relation to an encrypted programme that has been decoded without the lawful provider's authorisation` AND `the lawful provider or the owner of the copyright in the programme has thereby suffered loss or damage`

-- src:3772 | (3) An action must not be brought under subsection (1) or (2) after
-- src:3773 | the expiry of 6 years from the time the relevant act under
-- src:3774 | section 48(1) or (2) (as the case may be) took place.
@ref s 48A(3) (src:3772-3774)
-- READING (fork F-BA-04): "after the expiry of 6 years from the time the relevant act took place" is read on dates: an action
-- brought on or before the sixth anniversary of the day of the act is in time; one brought after it is not.
GIVEN `the day of the act` IS A NUMBER
      `the month of the act` IS A NUMBER
      `the year of the act` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the action is brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48A(3) the action is not barred` MEANS
    `the day the action is brought` AT MOST (Date `the day of the act` `the month of the act` (`the year of the act` PLUS 6))

§ `49. Offence of hindering employee or agent of Authority`

-- src:3778 | 49. Any person who obstructs or hinders any employee or agent of
-- src:3779 | the Authority acting in the discharge of the employee’s or agent’s
-- src:3780 | duty under this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:3781 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000.
@ref s 49 (guilt) (src:3778-3781)
GIVEN `the person obstructs or hinders an employee or agent of the Authority acting in the discharge of the employee's or agent's duty under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the person obstructs or hinders an employee or agent of the Authority acting in the discharge of the employee's or agent's duty under this Act`

-- src:3778 | 49. Any person who obstructs or hinders any employee or agent of
-- src:3779 | the Authority acting in the discharge of the employee’s or agent’s
-- src:3780 | duty under this Act shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:3781 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000.
@ref s 49 (punishment) (src:3778-3781)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 49 the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 5000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is provided`
                  , `daily fine` IS `no further daily fine is provided`
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

§ `50. Power of Authority to requisition information`

-- src:3788 | 50.—(1) The Authority or any person the Authority authorises in
-- src:3789 | that behalf may by notice require any person to provide the Authority
-- src:3790 | or the person so authorised, within the period specified in the notice,
-- src:3791 | with all such documents or information relating to all such matters as
-- src:3792 | the Authority may require for the purposes of this Act and as are
-- src:3793 | within that person’s knowledge or in that person’s custody or under
-- src:3794 | that person’s control.
@ref s 50(1) (src:3788-3794)
GIVEN `the Authority or a person it authorises has by notice required the document or information, within the period specified, for the purposes of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is within the person's knowledge, custody or control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(1) the person must provide the document or information` MEANS
    `the Authority or a person it authorises has by notice required the document or information, within the period specified, for the purposes of this Act` AND `it is within the person's knowledge, custody or control`

-- src:3796 | (2) Any person who, on being required by any notice under
-- src:3797 | subsection (1) to provide any document or information, fails to
-- src:3798 | comply with any requirement of the notice shall be guilty of an
-- src:3799 | offence.
@ref s 50(2) (src:3796-3799)
GIVEN `the person was required by a notice under subsection (1) to provide a document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with a requirement of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person was required by a notice under subsection (1) to provide a document or information` AND `the person fails to comply with a requirement of the notice`

-- src:3801 | (3) Any person who —
-- src:3803 | (a) intentionally alters, suppresses or destroys any document
-- src:3804 | which the person has been required by any notice under
-- src:3805 | subsection (1) to provide; or
-- src:3807 | (b) in providing any estimate, return or other information
-- src:3808 | required of the person under any notice under
-- src:3809 | subsection (1), makes any statement which the person
-- src:3810 | knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly
-- src:3811 | makes any statement which is false in a material particular,
-- src:3813 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 50(3) (src:3801-3813)
GIVEN `the person intentionally alters, suppresses or destroys a document the person was required by a notice to provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made a statement in the information required that the person knows to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person recklessly made a statement in the information required that is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person intentionally alters, suppresses or destroys a document the person was required by a notice to provide` OR `the person made a statement in the information required that the person knows to be false in a material particular` OR `the person recklessly made a statement in the information required that is false in a material particular`

-- src:3815 | (4) Any person guilty of an offence under subsection (2) or (3) shall
-- src:3816 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to
-- src:3817 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 50(4) (src:3815-3817)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 50(4) the punishment on conviction of an offence under subsection (2) or (3)` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 5000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `imprisonment not exceeding` 12
                  , `daily fine` IS `no further daily fine is provided`
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

§ `51. Power of police officer and other authorised persons against unlicensed broadcasting service or apparatus`

-- src:3822 | 51.—(1) Any police officer or any employee authorised by the
-- src:3823 | Authority may, if he or she has reasonable grounds for believing
-- src:3824 | that —
-- src:3826 | (a) a broadcasting service has been or is being provided in
-- src:3827 | contravention of this Act;
-- src:3832 | (b) a broadcasting service has been or is being provided in
-- src:3833 | breach of any licence; or
-- src:3835 | (c) any broadcasting apparatus used is not licensed by the
-- src:3836 | Authority,
-- src:3838 | enter and inspect any premises and seize any broadcasting apparatus
-- src:3839 | found in the premises which appears to be used for or in connection
-- src:3840 | with broadcasting.
@ref s 51(1) (src:3822-3840)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer or an employee authorised by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reasonable grounds for believing that a broadcasting service has been or is being provided in contravention of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reasonable grounds for believing that a broadcasting service has been or is being provided in breach of a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reasonable grounds for believing that broadcasting apparatus used is not licensed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(1) the person may enter and inspect the premises and seize broadcasting apparatus found there which appears to be used for or in connection with broadcasting` MEANS
    `the person is a police officer or an employee authorised by the Authority`
    AND (`the person has reasonable grounds for believing that a broadcasting service has been or is being provided in contravention of this Act` OR `the person has reasonable grounds for believing that a broadcasting service has been or is being provided in breach of a licence` OR `the person has reasonable grounds for believing that broadcasting apparatus used is not licensed by the Authority`)

-- src:3842 | (2) If there is no prosecution with regard to any broadcasting
-- src:3843 | apparatus seized under this section, such broadcasting apparatus is to
-- src:3844 | be taken and deemed to be forfeited to the Authority unless a claim is
-- src:3845 | made within 2 months from the date of seizure.
@ref s 51(2) (src:3842-3845)
GIVEN `there is no prosecution with regard to the apparatus seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim is made within 2 months from the date of seizure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(2) the apparatus is taken and deemed to be forfeited to the Authority` MEANS
    IF `there is no prosecution with regard to the apparatus seized` THEN JUST (NOT `a claim is made within 2 months from the date of seizure`) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3847 | (3) Any person asserting that the person is the owner of any
-- src:3848 | broadcasting apparatus so seized may personally or by the person’s
-- src:3849 | authorised agent give written notice to the Authority that the person
-- src:3850 | claims the broadcasting apparatus.
@ref s 51(3) (src:3847-3850)
GIVEN `the person asserts being the owner of the apparatus seized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(3) the person may, personally or by authorised agent, give written notice to the Authority that the person claims the apparatus` MEANS
    `the person asserts being the owner of the apparatus seized`

-- src:3852 | (4) On receiving the notice, the Authority may direct that the
-- src:3853 | broadcasting apparatus be released or may refer the matter to a
-- src:3854 | District Court or a Magistrate’s Court.
@ref s 51(4) (src:3852-3854)
GIVEN `the Authority has received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(4) the Authority may direct that the apparatus be released or refer the matter to a District Court or a Magistrate's Court` MEANS
    `the Authority has received the notice`

-- src:3856 | (5) The District Court or the Magistrate’s Court may proceed to the
-- src:3857 | examination of the matter and upon examination is to order that the
-- src:3858 | broadcasting apparatus be forfeited or released.
@ref s 51(5) (src:3856-3858)
GIVEN `the matter has been referred to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 51(5) the court is to examine the matter and, upon examination, order that the apparatus be forfeited or released` MEANS
    `the matter has been referred to the court`

§ `52. Power of arrest and search`

-- src:3862 | 52.—(1) The Chief Executive or any employee of the Authority the
-- src:3863 | Chief Executive authorises to act under this section may arrest
-- src:3864 | without warrant —
-- src:3866 | (a) any person found committing or attempting to commit or
-- src:3867 | employing or aiding any person to commit an arrestable
-- src:3868 | offence under this Act; or
-- src:3870 | (b) any person against whom a reasonable suspicion exists that
-- src:3871 | the person has been guilty of an arrestable offence under
-- src:3872 | this Act,
-- src:3877 | and may search any person so arrested, except that a female must not
-- src:3878 | be searched except by a female.
@ref s 52(1) (src:3862-3878)
GIVEN `the person is the Chief Executive or an employee of the Authority the Chief Executive authorises to act under the section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrestee is found committing, or attempting to commit, or employing or aiding a person to commit, an arrestable offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable suspicion exists that the arrestee has been guilty of an arrestable offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(1) the person may arrest the arrestee without warrant` MEANS
    `the person is the Chief Executive or an employee of the Authority the Chief Executive authorises to act under the section`
    AND (`the arrestee is found committing, or attempting to commit, or employing or aiding a person to commit, an arrestable offence under this Act` OR `a reasonable suspicion exists that the arrestee has been guilty of an arrestable offence under this Act`)

-- src:3877 | and may search any person so arrested, except that a female must not
-- src:3878 | be searched except by a female.
@ref s 52(1) the search of a person arrested (src:3877-3878)
GIVEN `the person arrested is a female` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person searching is a female` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(1) the arrested person may be searched by that searcher` MEANS
    (NOT `the person arrested is a female`) OR `the person searching is a female`

-- src:3882 | (2) Every person so arrested must, together with any article as to
-- src:3883 | which an offence may have been committed or attempted to be
-- src:3884 | committed, be taken to a police station.
@ref s 52(2) (src:3882-3884)
GIVEN `the person has been arrested under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(2) the person arrested must be taken, with any article as to which an offence may have been committed or attempted, to a police station` MEANS
    `the person has been arrested under this section`

-- src:3886 | (3) For the purposes of this section, offences punishable under
-- src:3887 | sections 30, 46, 47 and 48 are deemed to be arrestable offences within
-- src:3888 | the meaning of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010.
@ref s 52(3) (src:3886-3888)
GIVEN `the section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(3) an offence punishable under that section is deemed an arrestable offence within the meaning of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` MEANS
    `the section number of the offence` EQUALS 30 OR `the section number of the offence` EQUALS 46 OR `the section number of the offence` EQUALS 47 OR `the section number of the offence` EQUALS 48

§ `53. No entitlement to costs or damages`

-- src:3892 | 53. No person is entitled, in any proceedings before any court in
-- src:3893 | respect of any apparatus, equipment, article, book or document seized
-- src:3894 | in the exercise or the purported exercise of any power conferred under
-- src:3895 | this Act, to the costs of the proceedings or to any damages or other
-- src:3896 | relief other than an order for the return of the apparatus, equipment,
-- src:3897 | article, book or document or the payment of their value unless the
-- src:3898 | seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause.
@ref s 53 (src:3892-3898)
GIVEN `the seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53 the bar on costs, damages and other relief, save an order for return or payment of value, applies` MEANS
    NOT `the seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause`

§ `54. Offence against other laws`

-- src:3902 | 54. Nothing in this Act prevents any person —
-- src:3904 | (a) from being prosecuted under any other written law for any
-- src:3905 | act or omission which constitutes an offence under that
-- src:3906 | law; or
-- src:3908 | (b) from being liable under that other written law to any
-- src:3909 | punishment or penalty higher or other than that provided
-- src:3910 | by this Act,
-- src:3912 | but no person is to be punished twice for the same offence.
@ref s 54 (src:3902-3912)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence under another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has already been punished for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54 the person may be prosecuted under the other written law and be liable to its punishment or penalty, higher or other than this Act's` MEANS
    `the act or omission is an offence under another written law` AND (NOT `the person has already been punished for the same offence`)

§ `55. Conduct of proceedings by officers`

-- src:3916 | 55. Proceedings in respect of any offence under this Act may, with
-- src:3917 | the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor, be conducted by an officer
-- src:3918 | of the Authority or an officer of the Government authorised in writing
-- src:3919 | in that behalf by the Chief Executive.
@ref s 55 (src:3916-3919)
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor has authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the Authority, or an officer of the Government authorised in writing in that behalf by the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55 the person may conduct proceedings in respect of an offence under this Act` MEANS
    `the Public Prosecutor has authorised it` AND `the person is an officer of the Authority, or an officer of the Government authorised in writing in that behalf by the Chief Executive`

§ `56. Corporate offenders and unincorporated associations`

-- src:3928 | 56.—(1) Where an offence under this Act committed by a body
-- src:3929 | corporate is proved to have been committed with the consent or
-- src:3930 | connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of, an
-- src:3931 | officer of the body corporate, the officer as well as the body corporate
-- src:3932 | shall be guilty of that offence and shall be liable to be proceeded
-- src:3933 | against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 56(1) (src:3928-3933)
GIVEN `the offence was committed by a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that it was committed with the consent or connivance of, or attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(1) the officer as well as the body corporate is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    `the offence was committed by a body corporate` AND `it is proved that it was committed with the consent or connivance of, or attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer`

-- src:3935 | (2) Where the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its
-- src:3936 | members, subsection (1) applies in relation to the acts and defaults of
-- src:3937 | a member in connection with the member’s functions of management
-- src:3938 | as if the member were a director of the body corporate.
@ref s 56(2) (src:3935-3938)
GIVEN `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(2) subsection (1) applies to the acts and defaults of a member in connection with the member's functions of management as if the member were a director` MEANS
    IF `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3940 | (3) Proceedings for an offence alleged to have been committed
-- src:3941 | under this Act by an unincorporated association must be brought
-- src:3942 | against the association in its own name (and not in that of any of its
-- src:3943 | members) and, for the purposes of these proceedings, any rules of
-- src:3944 | court relating to service of documents have effect as if the association
-- src:3945 | were a corporation.
@ref s 56(3) (src:3940-3945)
GIVEN `the offence is alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(3) proceedings must be brought against the association in its own name and not in that of any of its members` MEANS
    IF `the offence is alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated association` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3947 | (4) Where an offence under this Act committed by a partnership is
-- src:3948 | proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or
-- src:3949 | to be attributable to any neglect on the part of, a partner, the partner as
-- src:3950 | well as the partnership shall be guilty of that offence and shall be
-- src:3951 | liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 56(4) (src:3947-3951)
GIVEN `the offence was committed by a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that it was committed with the consent or connivance of, or attributable to any neglect on the part of, a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(4) the partner as well as the partnership is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    `the offence was committed by a partnership` AND `it is proved that it was committed with the consent or connivance of, or attributable to any neglect on the part of, a partner`

-- src:3953 | (5) Where an offence under this Act committed by an
-- src:3954 | unincorporated association (other than a partnership) is proved to
-- src:3955 | have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be
-- src:3956 | attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer of the association
-- src:3957 | or a member of its governing body, the officer or member as well as
-- src:3958 | the association shall be guilty of that offence and shall be liable to be
-- src:3959 | proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 56(5) (src:3953-3959)
GIVEN `the offence was committed by an unincorporated association other than a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that it was committed with the consent or connivance of, or attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer of the association or a member of its governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(5) the officer or member as well as the association is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    `the offence was committed by an unincorporated association other than a partnership` AND `it is proved that it was committed with the consent or connivance of, or attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer of the association or a member of its governing body`

-- src:3961 | (6) Without limiting section 66, the Authority may make
-- src:3962 | regulations to provide for the application of any provision of this
-- src:3963 | section, with such modifications as the Authority considers
-- src:3964 | appropriate, to a body corporate or an unincorporated association
-- src:3965 | formed or recognised under the law of a country or territory outside
-- src:3966 | Singapore.
@ref s 56(6) (src:3961-3966)
GIVEN `the Authority has made regulations applying a provision of the section, with modifications it considers appropriate, to a body corporate or unincorporated association formed or recognised under the law of a country or territory outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(6) the section applies to the foreign body as the regulations provide` MEANS
    `the Authority has made regulations applying a provision of the section, with modifications it considers appropriate, to a body corporate or unincorporated association formed or recognised under the law of a country or territory outside Singapore`

-- src:3971 | (7) In this section —
-- src:3973 | “officer” —
-- src:3975 | (a) in relation to a body corporate, means a director,
-- src:3976 | member of the committee of management, chief
-- src:3977 | executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer
-- src:3978 | of the body corporate, or a person purporting to act in
-- src:3979 | any such capacity; or
@ref s 56(7) chapeau and "officer" of a body corporate (src:3971-3979)
GIVEN `it is a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person purporting to act in any such capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(7) the person is an officer in relation to a body corporate` MEANS
    `it is a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate` OR `it is a person purporting to act in any such capacity`

-- src:3981 | (b) in relation to an unincorporated association (other
-- src:3982 | than a partnership), means the president, the secretary
-- src:3983 | and members of the committee of the unincorporated
-- src:3984 | association and includes persons holding positions
-- src:3985 | analogous to those of president, secretary or member
-- src:3986 | of such a committee;
@ref s 56(7) "officer" of an unincorporated association (src:3981-3986)
GIVEN `it is the president, the secretary or a member of the committee of the association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it holds a position analogous to that of president, secretary or member of such a committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(7) the person is an officer in relation to an unincorporated association other than a partnership` MEANS
    `it is the president, the secretary or a member of the committee of the association` OR `it holds a position analogous to that of president, secretary or member of such a committee`

-- src:3988 | “partner” includes a person purporting to act as a partner.
@ref s 56(7) "partner" (src:3988)
GIVEN `the person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purports to act as a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56(7) the person is treated as a partner` MEANS
    `the person is a partner` OR `the person purports to act as a partner`

§ `57. Composition of offences`

-- src:3992 | 57.—(1) The Authority may compound any offence under this Act
-- src:3993 | which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting from the
-- src:3994 | person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum
-- src:3995 | not exceeding $1,000.
@ref s 57(1) (src:3992-3995)
-- The Authority may compound an offence PRESCRIBED as compoundable (by regulations under s 57(2)); the sum collected is not to exceed $1,000.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum the Authority collects from the person reasonably suspected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(1) the Authority may compound the offence by collecting that sum` MEANS
    `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` AND `the sum the Authority collects from the person reasonably suspected` AT MOST 1000

-- src:3997 | (2) The Authority may, with the approval of the Minister, make
-- src:3998 | regulations prescribing the offences which may be compounded.
@ref s 57(2) (src:3997-3998)
GIVEN `the Authority has made regulations, with the approval of the Minister, prescribing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 57(2) the offence has been prescribed as one which may be compounded` MEANS
    `the Authority has made regulations, with the approval of the Minister, prescribing the offence`

§ `58. Jurisdiction of court`

-- src:4002 | 58. Despite any provision to the contrary in the Criminal Procedure
-- src:4003 | Code 2010, a District Court and a Magistrate’s Court have
-- src:4004 | jurisdiction to try any offence under this Act and have power to
-- src:4005 | impose the full penalty or punishment in respect of the offence.
@ref s 58 (src:4002-4005)
GIVEN `the court is a District Court or a Magistrate's Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58 the court has jurisdiction to try an offence under this Act and power to impose the full penalty or punishment` MEANS
    `the court is a District Court or a Magistrate's Court`
